  "problem": "Given that $f(x)=2x$, the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ can be computed using the definition of the derivative. The first few steps of this calculation are shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{2(x+h)-2x}{h} \\\\  & =…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinish the calculation, and hence find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
